        "Every mason carves his own little mark on his stones. Look closely. You'll see them everywhere.",
        "The gargoyles are drainpipes, really. When it rains, they spit. That's their job.",
        "Change ringing: the bells go in patterns, never the same order twice. A full peal takes hours.",
        "The stained glass told the Bible stories to folk who couldn't read. Like a comic made of light.",
        "In the chained library, the books are chained to the shelves. Every book was worth a fortune, once.",
