      keeper: { name: 'THE GATE CAPTAIN', spr: 'guard' }, guardian: { name: 'THE OLD SOLDIER', spr: 'old_man_b' },
      trainers: [['ARCHER', 'archer', ['BREEZE', 'STONE']], ['SIGNALLER', 'redcoat', ['KINDLE', 'BREEZE']], ['BRICKMAKER', 'blacksmith', ['STONE', 'KINDLE']],
        ['DRUMMER', 'bard', ['CURRENT', 'STONE']], ['HORSE TRADER', 'merchant', ['LOAM', 'BREEZE']]],
      lost: ['SIGNAL FLAG', 'BRICK STAMP', 'BOW STRING', 'TEA BRICK', 'COPPER COIN'],
      folk: [
        "The wall wasn't built all at once. Different emperors built different bits, over hundreds of years.",
        "The beacon towers pass signals with smoke by day and fire by night. Faster than any horse.",
        "Some builders mixed sticky rice into the mortar. It sets harder than stone. Lunch and building, together.",
        "People say you can see the wall from the Moon. You can't. It's long but thin.",
        "Some bricks have the maker's name stamped on. If one cracks, they know whose door to knock on.",
        "The wall climbs right up the mountain ridges. My legs are very strong and very tired.",
        "The gate market's very busy. Horses from the north, tea and silk from the south.",
        "When I'm on night watch, the wall goes on and on in both directions, further than I can imagine.",
      ],
